n.</article-title><source><italic>Ann N Y Acad Sci.</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>1121</volume><fpage>499</fpage><lpage>527</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17872395</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Argyropoulos</surname><given-names>SV.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>SJ.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sleep disturbances in depression and the effects of antidepressants.</article-title><source><italic>Int Rev Psychiatry.</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>245</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16194795</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Armitage</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sleep and circadian rhythms in mood disorders.</article-title><source><italic>Acta Psychiatr Scand.</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>(suppl)</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>115</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giles</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jarrett</surname><given-names>RB.</given-names></name><name><surname>Roffwarg</surname><given-names>HP.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rush</surname><given-names>AJ.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reduced rapid eye moveme latency: a predictor of recurrence in depression.</article-title><source><italic>Neuropsychopharmacology.</italic></source><year>1987</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>39</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3509065</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Steiger</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Holsboer</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nocturnal secretion of prolactin and Cortisol and the sleep EEG in patients with major endogenous depression during an acute episode and after full remission.</article-title><source><italic>Psychiatry Res.</italic></source><year>1997</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9335199</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rush</surname><given-names>AJ.</given-names></name><name><surname>Erman</surname><given-names>MK.</given-names></name><name><surname>Giles</surname><given-names>DE.</given-names></name><name><surname>et al</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Polysomnographic findings in recently drug-free and clinically remitted depressed patients.</article-title><source><italic>Arch Gen Psychiatry.</italic></source><year>1986</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>878</fpage><lpage>884</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3753165</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref19"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Modell</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ising</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Holsboer</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauer</surname><given-names>CJ.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Munich Vulnerability Study on Affective Disorders: stability of polysomnographic findings over time.</article-title><source><italic>Biol Psychiatry.</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>430</fpage><lpage>437</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12242059</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Modell</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauer</surname><given-names>CJ.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rapid eye movement (REM) sleep: an endophenotype for depression.</article-title><source><italic>Curr Psychiatry Rep.</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>480</fpage><lpage>485</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18221628</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref21"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borbely</surname><given-names>AA.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A two-process model of sleep regulation.</article-title><source><italic>Hum Neurobiol.</italic></source><year>1982</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>195</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7185792</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dijk</surname><given-names>DJ.</given-names></name><name><surname>von Schantz</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Timing and consolidation of human sleep, wakefulness, and performance by a symphony of oscillators.</article-title><source><italic>J Biol Rhythms.</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>279</fpage><lpage>290</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16077148</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nutt</surname><given-names>DJ.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neurobiological mechanisms in generalized anxiety disorder.</article-title><source><italic>J Clin Psychiatry.</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>62 Suppl 11</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11414547</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref24"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jindal</surname><given-names>RD.</given-names></name><name><surname>Friedman</surname><given-names>ES.</given-names></name><name><surname>Berman</surname><given-names>SR.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fasiczka</surname><given-names>AL.</given-names></name><name><surname>Howland</surname><given-names>RH.</given-names></name><name><surname>Thase</surname><given-names>ME.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of sertraline on sleep architecture in patients with depression.</article-title><source><italic>J Clin Psychopharmacol.</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>540</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14624183</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref25"><label>25</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benedetti</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dallaspezia</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fulgosi</surname><given-names>MC.</given-names></name><name><surname>et al</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Actimetric evidence that CLOCK 3111 T/C SNP influences sleep and activity patterns in patients affected by bipolar depression.</article-title><source><italic>Am J Med Genet B Neuropsychiatr Genet.</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>144</volume><fpage>631</fpage><lpage>635</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17221848</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref26"><label>26</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Serretti</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cusin</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Benedetti</surname><given-names>F.</given-nam